<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <h2 id="t-sum-ledger-honest">Earned, Chosen, Owed, Testable</h2>
    <p>The most useful thing this page can do is tell you where to put your scepticism. Here is the whole
      framework sorted into four piles.</p>
    <div class="grid two">
      <div class="frame card">
        <h3>Earned &mdash; standard results, borrowed</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>ℵ&#8320; &lt; 2<sup>ℵ&#8320;</sup>, by Cantor's diagonal.</li>
          <li>Σ1/n diverges.</li>
          <li>d&sup2; = 0, and Stokes' theorem.</li>
          <li>The separatrix orbit has an infinite period.</li>
          <li>Pendulum phase space is a cylinder; the driven case is chaotic.</li>
          <li>Möbius topology: one side, one edge, Z&#8322;.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="frame card">
        <h3>Chosen &mdash; positions, argued not proved</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Existence requires only that nothing forbid it.</li>
          <li>π as the condition of a universe rather than a constant in one.</li>
          <li>The universe <em>is</em> the integration, not a thing integrated.</li>
          <li>dx as a completed act; the grain given, not chosen.</li>
          <li>A self as an operation rather than a thing.</li>
          <li>Polarity as accumulated residue.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="frame card">
        <h3>Owed &mdash; debts, stated as debts</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>The arrow.</strong> The step from Cantor's asymmetry to a physical direction of time
            is not rigorous, and the second law already does the job. This is the weakest joint in the
            structure.</li>
          <li><strong>The accumulation.</strong> Statistical mechanics derives temperature from molecular
            motion. The framework has no equivalent derivation.</li>
          <li><strong>The χ-field.</strong> Motivated, fitted, not derived from anything prior.</li>
          <li><strong>The mass ratio.</strong> 1836.15267343 remains unexplained by the proton-electron
            reading.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="frame card">
        <h3>Testable &mdash; and how it dies</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Galaxy handedness.</strong> The excess must survive correction for Doppler and
            selection bias, must reach 5σ, and its axis must <em>not</em> sit on our own galactic poles.
            Fail any of the three and the chapter is finished.</li>
          <li><strong>Proton decay.</strong> A detection strengthens the ledger's reading; an empty
            Hyper-Kamiokande era weakens it along with every grand unified theory.</li>
          <li><strong>Microtubule anaesthesia.</strong> The epothilone B result should replicate, or be
            withdrawn from the argument.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

